IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `scja-core`
IMPORT `scja3-sch3-third-schedule`

-- scja3-tests-sch3.l4: tests for the Third Schedule.  Expected values are written from the text of the Schedule
-- (SCJA1969.txt lines 5784-5828), beside each assertion, and not from the module's output.

§ `Tests: the Third Schedule`

-- A decision with the facts the Third Schedule turns on; every other field of Decision is a fixed placeholder that no rule here reads.
GIVEN court IS A Court
      about IS A `Subject of an order or application`
      way IS A `Way an order went`
GIVETH A Decision
`sch 3 test: a decision of the court on the subject, going that way` MEANS
    Decision WITH
        `made by` IS court
        `in the exercise of` IS `appellate jurisdiction`
        `nature of the proceeding` IS `a civil proceeding`
        `subject of the case` IS `any other civil matter`
        `the order` IS (Order OF about, way)
        `made after the trial of an action` IS FALSE
        `made by consent of the parties` IS FALSE
        `amount in dispute or value of the subject matter, excluding interest and costs` IS NOTHING
        `date made` IS Date 1 7 2024
        `date the judgment or order was extracted` IS NOTHING
        `a written law provides that it is final or that no appeal lies` IS FALSE
        `the parties agreed in writing, signed by or for each, that it is final` IS FALSE

`sch 3 test: DC gave unconditional permission to defend` MEANS `sch 3 test: a decision of the court on the subject, going that way` `District Court` `permission to defend proceedings` `granted unconditionally`
`sch 3 test: MC gave unconditional permission to defend` MEANS `sch 3 test: a decision of the court on the subject, going that way` `Magistrate's Court` `permission to defend proceedings` `granted unconditionally`
`sch 3 test: GD gave unconditional permission to defend` MEANS `sch 3 test: a decision of the court on the subject, going that way` `General Division` `permission to defend proceedings` `granted unconditionally`
`sch 3 test: DC gave conditional permission to defend` MEANS `sch 3 test: a decision of the court on the subject, going that way` `District Court` `permission to defend proceedings` `granted on condition that the party pays into court or gives security for the sum claimed`
`sch 3 test: DC refused permission to defend` MEANS `sch 3 test: a decision of the court on the subject, going that way` `District Court` `permission to defend proceedings` refused
`sch 3 test: DC set aside a default judgment unconditionally` MEANS `sch 3 test: a decision of the court on the subject, going that way` `District Court` `setting aside a default judgment` `granted unconditionally`
`sch 3 test: MC set aside a default judgment on condition` MEANS `sch 3 test: a decision of the court on the subject, going that way` `Magistrate's Court` `setting aside a default judgment` `granted on condition that the party pays into court or gives security for the sum claimed`
`sch 3 test: DC gave summary judgment` MEANS `sch 3 test: a decision of the court on the subject, going that way` `District Court` `summary judgment` `granted unconditionally`

-- case (a): an order giving unconditional permission to defend, by a District Court or Magistrate's Court
#ASSERT (`sch 3 case (a) the order gives unconditional permission to defend` `sch 3 test: DC gave unconditional permission to defend`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 3 case (a) the order gives unconditional permission to defend` `sch 3 test: MC gave unconditional permission to defend`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not a District Court or Magistrate's Court: the limb says "where a District Court or Magistrate's Court makes"
#ASSERT (`sch 3 case (a) the order gives unconditional permission to defend` `sch 3 test: GD gave unconditional permission to defend`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a conditional permission is case (b), not case (a)
#ASSERT (`sch 3 case (a) the order gives unconditional permission to defend` `sch 3 test: DC gave conditional permission to defend`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 3 case (a) the order gives unconditional permission to defend` `sch 3 test: DC refused permission to defend`) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- case (b): conditional permission to defend, except if the appellant is the party defending
#ASSERT (`sch 3 case (b) the order gives permission to defend on condition of payment into court or security` `sch 3 test: DC gave conditional permission to defend` FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 3 case (b) the order gives permission to defend on condition of payment into court or security` `sch 3 test: DC gave conditional permission to defend` TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 3 case (b) the order gives permission to defend on condition of payment into court or security` `sch 3 test: DC gave unconditional permission to defend` FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- case (c): unconditional setting aside of a default judgment
#ASSERT (`sch 3 case (c) the order sets aside a default judgment unconditionally` `sch 3 test: DC set aside a default judgment unconditionally`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 3 case (c) the order sets aside a default judgment unconditionally` `sch 3 test: MC set aside a default judgment on condition`) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- case (d): setting aside on condition, except if the appellant is the party against whom the judgment had been entered
#ASSERT (`sch 3 case (d) the order sets aside a default judgment on condition of payment into court or security` `sch 3 test: MC set aside a default judgment on condition` FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 3 case (d) the order sets aside a default judgment on condition of payment into court or security` `sch 3 test: MC set aside a default judgment on condition` TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 3 case (d) the order sets aside a default judgment on condition of payment into court or security` `sch 3 test: DC set aside a default judgment unconditionally` FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- the Schedule as a whole (seam 3): a case specified in the Third Schedule
#ASSERT (`sch 3 the decision is a case specified in the Third Schedule` `sch 3 test: DC gave unconditional permission to defend` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 3 the decision is a case specified in the Third Schedule` `sch 3 test: DC gave conditional permission to defend` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- conditional permission, and the appellant is the party defending: the exception takes it out, and no other limb holds
#ASSERT (`sch 3 the decision is a case specified in the Third Schedule` `sch 3 test: DC gave conditional permission to defend` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 3 the decision is a case specified in the Third Schedule` `sch 3 test: DC set aside a default judgment unconditionally` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 3 the decision is a case specified in the Third Schedule` `sch 3 test: MC set aside a default judgment on condition` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 3 the decision is a case specified in the Third Schedule` `sch 3 test: MC set aside a default judgment on condition` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a District Court decision that none of the four limbs lists
#ASSERT (`sch 3 the decision is a case specified in the Third Schedule` `sch 3 test: DC refused permission to defend` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 3 the decision is a case specified in the Third Schedule` `sch 3 test: DC gave summary judgment` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a decision of the General Division is outside the Schedule's scope: not covered
#ASSERT (`sch 3 the decision is a case specified in the Third Schedule` `sch 3 test: GD gave unconditional permission to defend` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

-- the effect: an appeal lies only with permission in a case the Schedule specifies; for any other case the Schedule is silent
#ASSERT (`sch 3 an appeal lies only with permission of that court or the General Division` `sch 3 test: DC gave unconditional permission to defend` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 3 an appeal lies only with permission of that court or the General Division` `sch 3 test: DC refused permission to defend` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`sch 3 an appeal lies only with permission of that court or the General Division` `sch 3 test: GD gave unconditional permission to defend` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

-- the limb helper on its own: any limb that holds gives JUST TRUE; none gives JUST FALSE; an unanswered limb gives NOTHING
#ASSERT (`sch 3 the limbs taken together` (LIST JUST FALSE, JUST TRUE)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 3 the limbs taken together` (LIST JUST FALSE, JUST FALSE)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 3 the limbs taken together` (LIST JUST FALSE, NOTHING)) EQUALS NOTHING
